[node name="Mesh" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="." unique_id=1501278172]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0)
editor_description = "GROUNDING OFFSET (story 3-0b, Pass 3b). The hero ROOT is the body CENTRE: Collision/HurtboxShape span root y [-1,+1] and main.tscn spawns both heroes at y 1.0, so the box floor rests exactly on the ground's top surface (y 0). The paladin FBX, however, has its origin at the model's FEET and was instanced with no transform in 3-0a, so the model sat a full half-box (1.0) ABOVE the box floor and visibly floated. This -1.0 puts the model's lowest vertex on the box floor. Only the model and FacingMarker are children of Mesh, so this moves nothing else; drive() assigns mesh.rotation.y, which preserves this origin. Pinned by test/integration/test_vertical_alignment.gd."

